From 065d1a7855e5fed453cf3c52ec1497081fb3c752 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Killy <308386066+killy-netsphere@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:06:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 008/211] N twin backends per device: every large-batch MoE
 split rotates over the twins

LLAMA_TWIN_BACKENDS=N creates N twins per GPU (ggml_backend_cuda_init_twin(device, k)); the primary keeps attention and
layer il uploads and computes its experts on twin il % N, so each upload runs under the previous layer GEMMs on another
stream. With one twin the primary own uploads waited behind its attention (+1-8 % only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
